---
title: Standing Hamstring & Calf Stretch
type: docs
prev: docs/rastyazhka/
---
![наклон к прямой ноге в полуприседе](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/40fa5fab-15fe-4c68-b426-0551b57ff2cf)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Stand upright and take a small step forward with your right foot.

### Step 2
Bend your back (left) knee slightly and keep your front (right) leg straight.

### Step 3
Point your right toes up toward the ceiling and hinge forward at your hips with a flat back, feeling the stretch in your hamstring, calf, and glutes.

### Step 4
Rest your hands gently on your thighs to support your upper body and deepen the stretch.

### Step 5
Hold this position for the recommended amount of time (usually 15–30 seconds).

### Step 6
Switch legs and repeat the stretch on the other side.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Try to keep the target muscles relaxed during the stretch.

• Breathe slowly and steadily.

• Do not force the stretch—stretch only until you feel comfortable tension, never sharp pain.
{{< /callout >}}
